---
/**
 * /about/corrections — the public corrections log.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';
import { href } from '../../lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Corrections"
  description="The public corrections log for Arthanomy — every material correction, when it was made, and why. How to report an error."
  path="/about/corrections"
>
  <header class="shell pt-10">
    <p class="eyebrow">Corrections</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 max-w-3xl font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The corrections log</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">
      Every material correction is logged here — what was wrong, what changed, and when. Corrections are made on the
      page itself and reflected in the article's updated date; this log is the record.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="shell mt-10 max-w-3xl pb-16">
    <div class="card overflow-hidden">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm">
        <caption class="sr-only">Log of published corrections</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-[var(--color-surface-2)]">
            <th scope="col" class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)] px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.05em] text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">Date</th>
            <th scope="col" class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)] px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.05em] text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">Where</th>
            <th scope="col" class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)] px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.05em] text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">Correction</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-4 align-top text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">2026-10-16</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4 align-top text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">
              <a href={href('/sources')} class="text-[var(--color-link)] underline decoration-1 underline-offset-2">Source registry</a>, and the
              articles citing the RBI Ombudsman
            </td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4 align-top">
              Four draft articles described the <strong>Reserve Bank – Integrated Ombudsman Scheme, 2021</strong> as the current
              grievance-redressal framework. The RBI's own FAQ, dated 1 July 2026, states that the
              <strong>Reserve Bank – Integrated Ombudsman Scheme, 2026</strong> came into force on that date and replaced the 2021
              scheme, which now governs only complaints received before 1 July 2026, appeals arising under it, and execution of
              its awards. The registry entry has been replaced with a dated <code class="font-mono text-xs">rbi-ombudsman-2026</code>
              source carrying the verified mechanics (entity-first requirement, the 30-day wait, the 90-day escalation window, the
              compensation limits and the appeal route), and the articles have been corrected. Not an error in any published
              article — the affected drafts had not been released, and the same check that found it also found the source-id
              collision logged below. Found by verifying a writer's own note rather than taking it on trust.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="whitespace-nowrap px-4 py-4 align-top text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">2026-10-16</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4 align-top text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">
              <a href={href('/sources')} class="text-[var(--color-link)] underline decoration-1 underline-offset-2">Source registry</a>, and ten briefs
            </td>
            <td class="px-4 py-4 align-top">
              The source id <code class="font-mono text-xs">bis-home</code> was doing two jobs: it pointed at the Bank for International
              Settlements, which is correct for the financial-mathematics and digital-assets briefs that cite it, and it was also
              attached to ten Indian gold, jewellery, diamond and construction-quality briefs, where "BIS" means the Bureau of
              Indian Standards. A separate <code class="font-mono text-xs">bis-india</code> source has been added (hallmarking
              regulation, Mandatory Hallmarking Order, jeweller registration, Quality Control Orders, National Building Code) and
              those ten briefs now require it. No reader-facing claim was affected — the affected article was written at
              mechanism level precisely because the source did not support it, and is being revised against the correct source.
              Found by an automated cross-check of brief source ids against source scope.
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-10 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold">How to report an error</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-7 text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">
      Email <a href={`mailto:${site.author.email}?subject=Correction`} class="text-[var(--color-link)] underline decoration-1 underline-offset-2">{site.author.email}</a>
      with the page, the sentence or figure in question, and — if you have one — the primary source you believe is
      correct. Reports citing official documents are actioned fastest. Every report gets a reply, whether or not it
      results in a change, and the reasoning is explained either way.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 font-serif text-2xl font-semibold">What counts as a correction</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">
      <li>Factual errors in figures, dates, provisions or product mechanics — always corrected and logged.</li>
      <li>Changed external facts (a tax rule superseded, a product closed) — updated with the change noted, not treated as an error.</li>
      <li>Disagreements about emphasis, prediction or opinion — discussed by email; not logged as corrections.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs leading-5 text-[var(--color-ink-faint)]">
      See also the <a href={href('/about/editorial-policy')} class="text-[var(--color-link)] underline decoration-1 underline-offset-2">editorial policy</a>
      and <a href={href('/about/methodology')} class="text-[var(--color-link)] underline decoration-1 underline-offset-2">methodology</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
